{"cuisine/banjar-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/banjar-cuisine","n":"Banjar cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Indonesia","intro":[["Banjarese cuisine is the cooking tradition and cuisine of Banjar people of South Kalimantan in Indonesia. Banjar cuisine is also found in neighbouring countries such as Brunei, Malaysia, and Singapore."],["Banjar cuisine has been influenced by many cultures, includes Malay, Javanese, Chinese and Indian cuisine."],["One of the famous culinary of Banjar cuisine is soto banjar. Soto banjar has become one of Indonesia's special foods that are already very well known and recognised by many people. Soto banjar is served in many restaurants throughout the province. Soto banjar is a soto made from chicken meat as its main ingredient, then added with various spices such as onion, white onion, cumin, fennel, and cinnamon to make the soto more savoury. Additional juice from lime makes this dish even more fresh. This dish is usually served during lunchtime."],["Banjar cuisine generally includes soupy foods like sop ayam banjar. Unlike soto banjar, which uses ketupat, the chicken soup is served with steamed rice. The broth is made with spices like clove, star anise, nutmeg and ginger. Companions to this dish can include rice vermicelli, a sprinkle of fried shallots, a spring onion, and lime juice."],["Ketupat Kandangan Banjar is a speciality of South Kalimantan which is usually associated with the Muslim holy day of Eid al-Fitr. It originated from Kandangan, South Hulu Sungai Regency. The food can usually be found around the Muslim holy month of Ramadan. What distinguishes this dish from the usual ketupat is that ketupat kandangan banjar use the tuna as its main ingredient. Sometime it would also use a baked cork fish and cooked with yellow coconut milk sauce. The spices used are from cinnamon, cloves, and cardamom. It tastes savoury and is suitable for eating during the day or breakfast."],["Kue bingka is a cake (kue) that unique to the Banjarese. It feels very sweet, fat, and soft. Bingka is one of the cakes used in the Banjar tradition to serve 41 types of cakes for special occasions such as weddings. Although it can be found throughout the year, bingka is usually common in Ramadan because it is considered suitable for breaking the fast. Bingka is made of flour, eggs, coconut milk, sugar and salt. As a rule, bingka is baked with floral prints. There are various kinds of bingka such as bingka tapai, bingka kentang, bingka labu, bingka pandan and so forth. In addition, there are other types of bingka which are common during Ramadan, namely bingka barandam which is actually quite different from the usual bingka. Aside from being a typical Banjarese dessert, bingka is also famous in neighbouring provinces such as East Kalimantan and Central Kalimantan, even to foreign countries such as Malaysia and Brunei Darussalam."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"banjar-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banjar_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/33/Penjual_Jajanan_Tradisional_Banjar_di_Halong.JPG/500px-Penjual_Jajanan_Tradisional_Banjar_di_Halong.JPG","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ezagren (bicara / talk)","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Penjual_Jajanan_Tradisional_Banjar_di_Halong.JPG"}},"dish/agliata":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/agliata","n":"Agliata","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Agliata is a pungent, savoury garlic sauce and condiment in Italian cuisine used to flavour and accompany grilled or boiled meats, fish and vegetables. It is first attested in ancient Rome, and it remains part of the cuisine of Liguria. Porrata is a similar sauce prepared with leeks in place of garlic."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-agliata"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agliata"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carpaccio","dish/carpaccio"],["Cassatella di sant'Agata","dish/cassatella-di-sant-agata"],["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"],["Ciabatta","dish/ciabatta"],["Cioppino","dish